## Context

The full `make check` after the 0875 identity-split merge fails four existing
country migration tests. `scripts/jetp/_country_migration.py:87`
(`legacy_dispositions`) raises `ValueError: Unclassified country input:
agreements.csv` or `documents.csv` while scanning `data/jetp/`. Both files
already exist on main at `c92e62b9`; neither the 0876 nor 0884 branch adds
them. The temporary country migration readers should distinguish their own
legacy inputs from the ontology-v2 ledger tables introduced by the train.

The separate `test_jetp_courbe_reference` failure in these fresh worktrees is
an absent `data/jetp/crs` DVC checkout, not this code defect.

## Work

- Reproduce the four country migration failures on main with the required
  local data present.
- Make the legacy-input scanner classify the new ledger tables explicitly,
  without hiding an unknown country-specific file.
- Keep the country staging outputs and served views byte-identical.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] IDN, SEN, VNM and ZAF migration tests pass with the ontology-v2 tables present.
- [ ] An unknown extra input still fails with a named error.
- [ ] Country staging outputs and served views are byte-identical before and after.
- [ ] `make check-fast`, `make lint` and full `make check` pass with the CRS DVC dataset materialized.
